  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The words \"there is\" indicate we use an existential quantifier, $\u2203.$\n\n- The sentence refers to prime numbers. So, by denoting a prime number as $p,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\u2203\\,p\\text{\u00a0prime}.\n$$\n\n- \"One more than its double\" can be written as $2p+1,$ so the condition in the statement can be written as\n\n$$\n2p+1\\text{\u00a0is prime.}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows:\n\n$\u2203\\,p$ prime, $2p+1$ is prime.",
